+        "hypothesis": "The Phase 1 anomaly suggested that a logged-in low-privileged user could abuse the rating AJAX endpoint.",
+        "trace": "The handler checks the nonce, resolves the current session's user ID, and writes a single boolean-like marker into that same user's suretriggers_rating_clicked meta key.",
+        "defenses": "There is no caller-controlled target user ID and no cross-user update sink. Unauthenticated callers cannot access the route.",
+        "refutation": "I looked for any place where the endpoint accepts an arbitrary user identifier or writes to options, posts, or files instead of the current user's own metadata and found none.",
+        "conclusion": "At most, a logged-in user can dismiss their own plugin-row rating prompt. That is not a reportable security impact."
+      },
+      "reopen_conditions": "Reopen if a future change lets the caller specify another user's ID or reaches a more sensitive sink than the current user's own meta key."
+    },
+    {
+      "finding_id": "NEG-007",
+      "verdict": "FP",
+      "state": "REJECTED",
