+          "note": "The AJAX handler rejects requests without a valid suretrigger_form nonce."
+        },
+        {
+          "file_path": "plugins/suretriggers/functions.php",
+          "line_number": 301,
+          "note": "After nonce validation, the handler emits the st_trigger_button_action hook that powers the feature."
+        },
+        {
+          "file_path": "plugins/suretriggers/src/Integrations/triggerbutton/triggers/user-clicks-on-trigger-button.php",
+          "line_number": 69,
+          "note": "The integration registers st_trigger_button_action as the common trigger hook."
+        },
+        {
+          "file_path": "plugins/suretriggers/src/Integrations/triggerbutton/triggers/user-clicks-on-trigger-button.php",
+          "line_number": 112,
+          "note": "The trigger listener routes the event into AutomationController::sure_trigger_handle_trigger() as the documented automation feature."
+        }
+      ],
+      "reasoning": {
+        "hypothesis": "The public trigger-button surface might let arbitrary visitors execute privileged actions or abuse the pre-nonce do_action() call.",
+        "trace": "The shortcode intentionally exposes a trigger form. The AJAX endpoint validates the shortcode nonce at functions.php:278-280 and then emits st_trigger_button_action at functions.php:301, which the bundled trigger integration consumes as the user-click trigger.",
+        "defenses": "The feature is intentionally public when the site owner embeds the shortcode. The in-plugin sink is the automation trigger path itself, not an option write, file operation, or privileged admin mutation. The public redirect values are returned through esc_url_raw().",
+        "refutation": "I searched the repository for listeners on st_trigger_button_before_click_hook and st_trigger_button_after_click_hook and found no bundled add_action()/add_filter() registrations that make the pre-nonce do_action() security-relevant. The only bundled listener tied to this surface is the documented automation trigger registration on st_trigger_button_action.",
+        "conclusion": "This is intended functionality. The mere existence of a public automation trigger chosen by the site owner is not, by itself, an authorization flaw."
+      },
+      "reopen_conditions": "Reopen if a bundled addon or future release attaches a sensitive callback to st_trigger_button_before_click_hook or if the shortcode becomes reachable in a role context that should not be able to trigger automations."
+    },
+    {
+      "finding_id": "NEG-006",
+      "verdict": "FP",
+      "state": "REJECTED",
+      "title": "Rating-clicked AJAX endpoint only mutates the current user's own metadata",
+      "entry_point_ids": [
+        "ep_ajax_priv_wp_ajax_suretriggers_rating_clicked"
+      ],
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "file_path": "plugins/suretriggers/functions.php",
+          "line_number": 167,
+          "note": "The route is authenticated-only; there is no nopriv registration."
+        },
+        {
+          "file_path": "plugins/suretriggers/functions.php",
+          "line_number": 176,
+          "note": "The endpoint requires a suretriggers_rating_nonce nonce."
+        },
+        {
+          "file_path": "plugins/suretriggers/functions.php",
+          "line_number": 181,
+          "note": "The sink is update_user_meta(get_current_user_id(), 'suretriggers_rating_clicked', true)."
+        }
+      ],
+      "reasoning": {
+        "hypothesis": "The Phase 1 anomaly suggested that a logged-in low-privileged user could abuse the rating AJAX endpoint.",
+        "trace": "The handler checks the nonce, resolves the current session's user ID, and writes a single boolean-like marker into that same user's suretriggers_rating_clicked meta key.",
+        "defenses": "There is no caller-controlled target user ID and no cross-user update sink. Unauthenticated callers cannot access the route.",
+        "refutation": "I looked for any place where the endpoint accepts an arbitrary user identifier or writes to options, posts, or files instead of the current user's own metadata and found none.",
+        "conclusion": "At most, a logged-in user can dismiss their own plugin-row rating prompt. That is not a reportable security impact."
+      },
+      "reopen_conditions": "Reopen if a future change lets the caller specify another user's ID or reaches a more sensitive sink than the current user's own meta key."
+    },
+    {
+      "finding_id": "NEG-007",
+      "verdict": "FP",
+      "state": "REJECTED",
+      "title": "admin_init connection-save path is protected by a connect nonce and administrator capability",
+      "entry_point_ids": [
+        "ep_admin_init_admin_init"
+      ],
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "file_path": "plugins/suretriggers/src/Controllers/AuthController.php",
+          "line_number": 92,
+          "note": "AuthController::save_connection() is reachable on admin_init."
+        },
+        {
+          "file_path": "plugins/suretriggers/src/Controllers/AuthController.php",
+          "line_number": 104,
+          "note": "The handler exits unless sure-trigger-connect-nonce verifies."
+        },
+        {
+          "file_path": "plugins/suretriggers/src/Controllers/AuthController.php",
+          "line_number": 108,
+          "note": "The handler also exits unless current_user_can('administrator')."
+        },
+        {
+          "file_path": "plugins/suretriggers/src/Controllers/AuthController.php",
+          "line_number": 120,
+          "note": "Only after those checks does the code reach SaasApiToken::save() and OptionController::set_option()."
+        }
+      ],
+      "reasoning": {
+        "hypothesis": "Because admin_init is broadly reachable in WordPress, a lower-privileged user might be able to set or reset the OttoKit connection through query parameters.",
+        "trace": "The admin_init handler reads GET parameters, validates the connect nonce at AuthController.php:104-105, validates the administrator capability at AuthController.php:108-109, and only then saves the access key and connected email at AuthController.php:120-123.",
+        "defenses": "Both a valid connect nonce and the administrator role/capability marker are required before any connection-state write occurs.",
+        "refutation": "I traced the nonce source back to Loader::get_localized_array() at Loader.php:515. Although delegated OttoKit viewers can receive UI data, the sink itself still rejects them because save_connection() requires current_user_can('administrator').",
+        "conclusion": "The admin_init path is not a low-privilege connection takeover in the shipped plugin."
+      },
+      "reopen_conditions": "Reopen if a bundled path lets non-admin users satisfy the administrator check or if the connect nonce becomes exposed in a reusable admin context without the corresponding privilege boundary."
+    }
