codex
`Phase 2` report is written to [reports/phase2/suretriggers-phase2.codex.json](/Volumes/External_Disk/timo/WORDPRESS-PLUGIN-RESEARCH/reports/phase2/suretriggers-phase2.codex.json).

Result: `0` TP, `0` REVIEW, `7` FP, `1` out-of-scope note, overall risk `low`. The public-facing candidates were refuted by concrete guards or intended behavior: `suretriggers_save_settings` is split into an error-only `nopriv` hook plus an admin+nonce writer, `connection/create-wp-connection` still requires an administrator application password and SaaS token verification, `api-test` is only a fixed-string health check, and the trigger-button flow is an intended public automation trigger rather than an unintended privilege boundary.

The JSON is valid and I verified the final counts with `jq`.
